      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's getting pretty intense. if the whole constellation is acting as a distributed engine, that would explain why we can't catch a single \"source\" of the signal—it's literally everywhere and nowhere at the same time.\n\ni was looking at the \"instruction\" part of it again. if they're using the constellation to decrypt or route these messages, it implies a level of control over the orbital software that most people think is impossible. \n\nif someone actually had that kind of access, what would be the endgame? would they be using this to coordinate movements of \"dark\" assets in orbit, or is this just a way to maintain a shadow network that exists entirely outside of any government's oversight? i'm trying to understand the scale of what we're actually looking at here.",
